---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# (Terminal states are real: the child exited after its one respawn.)
# An open tools.ask across a ui/ask row remount (hot reload, /model swap)
# and across the child's exit and respawn. Recipe: go/tests/model/README.md.
# The single-process, single-mount flow is ask_answer.fizz; this one
# adds what that one takes as fixed: the Asker, the headless answer
# router and the ask ids all belong to one mount of one process.
#
# Where each piece lives in the code:
#   Asker    plugins/ask/ask.go: one per ask-row Apply. pending[id] holds
#            the blocked call; ids are "ask-"+seq from a counter that
#            starts at 0 in every Asker (putIn).
#   router   plugins/ui/headless.go: hlAsk (the id the next stdin line
#            answers, set by hlPrint on the "ask" event) and hlAnswer
#            (the current mount's "ask-answers", nil between dispose and
#            remount: runHeadless's disposer). hlAnswerPending clears
#            hlAsk and calls hlAnswer.Answer(hlAsk.id, line).
#   serve    internal/serve/supervisor.go s.asks (armed): set on "ask",
#            cleared by Answer (after the stdin write) and by
#            done/cancelled/error/exit/result/call. api.go answer
#            refuses {ask} only when it names a different pending id.
#   page     app.tsx: the composer draft and draftAsk, both kept in
#            localStorage per session, so they survive a page reload;
#            askChanged = draftAsk !== row.ask.id holds Send back.
#
# Fields. alive: a child process. gen: which Asker is current (the ask
# row's Apply count across processes). seq: that Asker's counter.
# uiUp: the ui row is mounted (hlAnswer set). open/openId/openGen: the
# ask call that is blocked, which Asker holds it. hlAsk: the router's
# pending id. held: an answer line that reached the child in the gap
# ("" | "ans" | "sec"), heldSrc the question it was written for. armed:
# serve's arm. row/rowQ/rowSecret: the ask the page shows. draft/draftId:
# the composer draft (the question it was written for) and its draftAsk.
# used: every ask id this session's history has. q1 and q2 are the two
# questions the model asks (each once), plain or secret.
#
# The last four fields are ghosts, sticky once set, for the invariants:
# answerAsPrompt (an answer line reached the loop as user input),
# secretAsInput (a secret did), dupId (an ask id repeated in history),
# wrongAnswer (an answer written for one question answered another).
#
# THIS SPEC IS THE INTENDED BEHAVIOUR. The product differs in three
# places (findings; each is the mutation that makes an invariant fail):
#  1. Gap (Deliver with not uiUp): hlAnswerPending sees hlAnswer nil,
#     drops hlAsk and returns false, so the line falls through to
#     hlSubmit, which waits for the remount and sends it as a prompt.
#     A secret too: `secret && hlAnswerPending` fails the same way.
#     Intended: the line is held and handed to the remounted router,
#     which answers the ask or refuses the line; never a prompt.
#  2. ReloadAsk: the ask row's Apply has no effect for pending asks, so
#     the blocked call keeps waiting on the old Asker. The ui row
#     remounts with the new Asker, whose pending map is empty: the next
#     answer is disarmed by serve, refused by the new Asker ("no pending
#     ask") and lost, while the page still shows the question with
#     nothing armed (409 on every retry) until the 10-minute timeout.
#     Intended: disposing an Asker ends its open asks at once (the call
#     returns an error, the call/result event disarms serve and clears
#     the row), so the page is told.
#  3. Ids: every Asker restarts at ask-1, both after ReloadAsk and in
#     a respawned child. Intended: ids unique per session history
#     (gen-qualified here). With reused ids a draft kept (localStorage)
#     for the old ask-1 matches the new ask-1: askChanged is false, the
#     api's id check passes, and it answers a different question.

role Session:
    action Init:
        self.alive = True
        self.gen = 1
        self.seq = 0
        self.reloads = 0
        self.respawns = 0
        self.uiUp = True
        self.asked = 0
        self.open = ""
        self.openId = ""
        self.openGen = 0
        self.hlAsk = ""
        self.held = ""
        self.heldSrc = ""
        self.armed = ""
        self.row = ""
        self.rowQ = ""
        self.rowSecret = False
        self.draft = ""
        self.draftId = ""
        self.used = []
        self.answerAsPrompt = False
        self.secretAsInput = False
        self.dupId = False
        self.wrongAnswer = False

    # The model calls tools.ask / tools.secret. The event reaches the
    # headless printer only while the ui row is mounted (a disposed
    # mount's broadcaster stops publishing), so asks start with it up.
    atomic action AskPlain:
        require self.alive and self.uiUp and self.open == "" and self.held == "" and self.asked < 2
        self.put(False)

    atomic action AskSecret:
        require self.alive and self.uiUp and self.open == "" and self.held == "" and self.asked < 2
        self.put(True)

    # Config hot reload of the ui row: dispose, then remount later. In
    # between hlAnswer is nil.
    atomic action ReloadUi:
        require self.alive and self.uiUp
        self.uiUp = False

    atomic fair action RemountUi:
        require self.alive and not self.uiUp
        self.uiUp = True
        if self.held != "":
            self.route(self.heldSrc)
            self.held = ""
            self.heldSrc = ""

    # The ask row remounts (a /model swap remounts rows that register
    # tools on codemode; Park frees the VM for it during an ask). The ui
    # row Gets "ask-answers", so it remounts too: a gap opens.
    atomic action ReloadAsk:
        require self.alive and self.uiUp and self.reloads < 1
        self.reloads += 1
        self.gen += 1
        self.seq = 0
        self.uiUp = False
        if self.open != "":
            # Intended: the disposed Asker cancels what it holds.
            self.resolve()

    # The person answers the question on screen through its own control
    # (an option, the answer field, the secret field): POST /answer with
    # the row's id.
    atomic action Answer:
        require self.alive and self.row != "" and self.armed == self.row
        self.deliver(self.rowQ, self.rowSecret)

    # Typing into the composer while a plain question is on screen
    # starts an answer draft, keyed to that question's id (draftAsk).
    atomic action TypeDraft:
        require self.draft == "" and self.row != "" and not self.rowSecret
        self.draft = self.rowQ
        self.draftId = self.row

    # askChanged note: "Use for this question" retargets the draft on
    # the person's say-so.
    atomic action UseForQuestion:
        require self.draft != "" and self.row != "" and not self.rowSecret and self.draftId != self.row
        self.draft = self.rowQ
        self.draftId = self.row

    # Send: only when askChanged is false; POST /answer {ask: draftId}.
    atomic action SendDraft:
        require self.draft != "" and self.alive and self.row != "" and self.draftId == self.row and self.armed == self.row
        src = self.draft
        self.draft = ""
        self.draftId = ""
        self.deliver(src, False)

    # tools.ask's timeout: the call returns an error, the call/result
    # event disarms serve and clears the row.
    atomic fair action Timeout:
        require self.alive and self.open != ""
        self.resolve()

    # The child exits (crash, restart) and a later prompt respawns it:
    # a fresh process, a fresh ui mount and Asker. What was in flight in
    # the old one (an open ask, a held line) is gone; the draft stays.
    atomic action Exit:
        require self.alive
        self.alive = False
        self.open = ""
        self.openId = ""
        self.openGen = 0
        self.hlAsk = ""
        self.held = ""
        self.heldSrc = ""
        self.armed = ""
        self.row = ""
        self.rowQ = ""
        self.rowSecret = False
        self.uiUp = True

    atomic action Respawn:
        require not self.alive and self.respawns < 1
        self.respawns += 1
        self.alive = True
        self.gen += 1
        self.seq = 0

    atomic func put(secret):
        self.asked += 1
        self.seq += 1
        id = "g" + str(self.gen) + "-ask-" + str(self.seq)
        if id in self.used:
            self.dupId = True
        self.used = self.used + [id]
        q = "q" + str(self.asked)
        self.open = q
        self.openId = id
        self.openGen = self.gen
        self.hlAsk = id
        self.armed = id
        self.row = id
        self.rowQ = q
        self.rowSecret = secret

    # serve writes the line and disarms; the child reads it.
    atomic func deliver(src, secret):
        self.armed = ""
        if not self.uiUp:
            if secret:
                self.held = "sec"
            else:
                self.held = "ans"
            self.heldSrc = src
        else:
            self.route(src)

    # hlAnswerPending: the current Asker answers the router's id, or the
    # line is refused (an error line); either way hlAsk clears.
    atomic func route(src):
        if self.hlAsk != "" and self.hlAsk == self.openId and self.openGen == self.gen:
            if src != self.open:
                self.wrongAnswer = True
            self.open = ""
            self.openId = ""
            self.openGen = 0
            self.row = ""
            self.rowQ = ""
            self.rowSecret = False
        self.hlAsk = ""

    atomic func resolve():
        self.open = ""
        self.openId = ""
        self.openGen = 0
        self.hlAsk = ""
        self.armed = ""
        self.row = ""
        self.rowQ = ""
        self.rowSecret = False

action Init:
    session = Session()

# An answer line is never submitted as a prompt: with no Asker to take
# it, it is held or refused.
always assertion AnswerNeverPrompt:
    return not session.answerAsPrompt

# A secret never becomes an input entry.
always assertion SecretNeverInput:
    return not session.secretAsInput

# Ask ids are unique within a session's history, across remounts and
# processes.
always assertion AskIdsUnique:
    return not session.dupId

# A draft written for one ask answers that ask only.
always assertion DraftReachesItsAsk:
    return not session.wrongAnswer

# The question on screen can still be answered: serve holds its arm, or
# its answer is on its way (held in the gap, or already written).
always assertion ShownAskAnswerable:
    return session.row == "" or session.armed == session.row or session.held != ""

# An ask that survives a remount is answered or ends (timeout, cancel,
# exit), and a line held in the gap is handed on.
always eventually assertion AskEnds:
    return session.open == ""

always eventually assertion HeldHandedOn:
    return session.held == ""
